WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.630
So I left California and moved to Florida.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.000
After 14 transformational
years in Los Angeles

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.410
where we built careers, bought a house,

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.340
got married and had three kids,

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:15.490
my wife, Lindsey, and I decided
to pack up and relocate.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.180
And we're not alone.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.460
California's approach to the
pandemic made life here harder

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.940
than ever before.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:25.060
I've reported extensively
on California's policies,

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.980
from the expensive and
unreliable energy grid

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.500
to the aggressive taxation and regulation,

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.100
from the draconian lockdowns

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.370
that permanently damaged all businesses

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:35.780
and kept children out of school

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.650
for longer than anywhere else

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.550
to the failure of city leaders to cope

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:41.240
with the nation's worst homelessness

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.700
and mental health crises.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.050
Yeah, I've seen it all firsthand.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:48.200
But my reasons for moving
aren't primarily political;

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.730
they're personal.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:52.210
And California, I still love you.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:55.710
Sometimes I really don't, but, yeah, I do.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:01.200
14 years ago, my future
wife's Honda Accord hustled us

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.130
2,400 miles in three days
so that she could make it

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.290
for a job interview in Los Angeles.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.830
We left behind friends,
family, and Florida,

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.940
trading the swamps of the Sunshine State

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:12.560
for the glamor of Hollywood.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:14.130
We memorialized the moment

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:17.110
with blurry digital photos
snapped from the car window.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.250
We soaked in the famous SoCal weather,

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.210
so consistently pleasant that
the outdoors anywhere else

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:24.060
just never quite lives up to it.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.750
We gawked at the natural beauty

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.550
and gorged ourselves on the rich,

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.660
varigated culture of Los Angeles,

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.110
a city packed full of people

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.520
creative, daring, and delusional enough

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:34.830
to follow their dreams.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.830
My kids are all California natives,

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.160
and life there on balance was good to me.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:42.060
They trounce through mountain
streams in the Sierras,

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.390
hid inside centenarian redwoods,

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:47.160
splashed at the edge of
the vast cold Pacific,

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.220
played and learned alongside other kids

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:50.420
from around the world,

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:52.720
learned how to count
Mandarin, greet in Spanish,

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:54.703
and express their gratitude in Korean.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.670
Then things started to change
both for us and in the world.

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:04.600
Beijing tries to show it's in control

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.770
of the epidemic consuming this country.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:08.620
Coronavirus officially hitting the US.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:09.710
Coronavirus now classified

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.870
as a public health emergency.
Coronavirus forcing millions

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:13.833
more Americans into virtual lockdown.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:16.878
Over 75 million people
in New York, California,

00:02:16.878 --> 00:02:18.961
Vermont, and Connecticut-

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.950
I've never seen so much open road on I10

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.540
as I did this Sunday
morning in March 2020.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.880
Stay at home, 15 days
to flatten the curve.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.470
As the dynamism of L.A. ground to a halt,

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:33.630
the smog cleared, the birds chirped,

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.730
and we would see and hear our surroundings

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.910
in a way we never had before.

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:40.000
It made us look at California differently.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.140
The upsides and downsides each
coming into sharper focus.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:46.300
The rolling blackouts are more unsettling

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.150
and the wildfire smoke more oppressive

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.690
when you're already stuck in your house

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.550
or compelled to wear a
mask once you step outside.

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:54.840
Gavin Newsom blames climate change,

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.420
but his policies matter too.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.370
The forests weren't properly managed

00:02:58.370 --> 00:02:59.700
and the increasingly solar

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.760
and wind-dependent grid is fragile.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.610
Newsom personally hastened the closure

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:05.670
of California's last nuclear plant.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:07.340
When Germany closed all of theirs,

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:09.930
emissions went up and so did prices.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:12.330
My oldest son was still
in preschool last year

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.400
so he was spared much of the frustration

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.350
and social isolation of remote learning

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:17.980
that so many experienced.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:18.840
But it was disturbing

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.800
to watch California
keep its schools closed

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.480
long after other countries
and states were demonstrating

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.200
that safe in-person
schooling was possible.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.780
The governor's own kids attended
private school in-person

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:31.210
while most public school
campuses stayed empty.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.510
The powerful teacher's
unions used their positions

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:35.930
to extract hundreds of
millions of additional dollars

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.000
during the shutdown.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.100
And L.A.'s union issued a list of demands

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.390
that included a wealth
tax, Medicare for all,

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:43.470
and abandoned all new charter schools.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:46.760
School's back now with
mandatory weekly testing,

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.820
social distancing, mandatory masking

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:50.240
for even the fully vaccinated,

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:53.010
and vaccine mandates
for all eligible kids.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:54.730
And the situation on the streets,

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.230
already bad before COVID, only got worse

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:58.940
as L.A. Mayor Eric Garcetti's

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:01.790
underperforming $1.2 billion plan

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:04.370
to build homeless housing
completely stalled.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:07.450
And the city faced a violent
crime and homicide spike.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:10.530
I voted for and still
support sentencing reform.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.730
I believe no person should
be jailed for drugs,

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.530
and think we need a social
safety net of some kind

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.610
for those who can't
take care of themselves.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.960
But a city also needs the rule of law

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.870
and safe public spaces to function,

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.160
and many of California's
big cities are failing

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.350
on those fronts.

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:28.310
The city's cultural and
culinary life nearly died

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:29.600
as we shelter in place.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:33.070
It's coming back in its own
socially distanced, masked,

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:35.200
and mandatory-vaccine-verified way.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.660
But for many small businesses,

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:38.690
there will be no second life.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:41.520
Shutting down outdoor
dining without any grounding

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:44.260
in science evidence or
logic is one judge ruling

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.887
against the forest closures put it,

00:04:45.887 --> 00:04:48.600
"Ended the California dream
for many restaurateurs."

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.390
And yet California's political class seems

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.920
more secure than ever.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:54.590
L.A.'s mayor has failed upward

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:56.130
towards a US ambassadorship.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:58.250
The governor survived recall easily,

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.460
and the Democratic
supermajority is rushing

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:03.040
to make future recalls an impossibility.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.600
And when one party rules,

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.340
those who've captured that
party can make the rules.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.480
Teachers unions, firefighter
unions, prison guard unions,

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:12.430
state service employee unions.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:14.730
Public sector unions feed public money

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:15.950
and power to themselves

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:19.150
so they can continually increase
that power and influence,

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:21.800
allowing them to feed more
money and power to themselves.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.010
What about my power and your power

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:27.677
to make our own choices
about our own lives?

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.130
But as my moving date drew closer,

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.830
a new feeling washed over,

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:36.870
a blissful attachment
from California politics.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:38.230
When your voice goes unheard,

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.660
it's sometimes better
to head for the exit.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:43.550
But again, my move isn't purely political.

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:45.650
If it were, I might be in
New Hampshire right now,

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:48.050
surrounded by more of the like-minded.

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:51.020
Most of life isn't about
politics, thankfully.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:53.710
See, people I love are in Florida,

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:55.400
and they're getting older as am I.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.330
And it's a new world with new rules

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:00.130
where you can more easily live
and work from where you want.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.400
And I still love you, California.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:05.410
I made my career, my
home, and my family here.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:06.720
I'll miss California.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:10.800
Despite politics, this is still
a spectacularly beautiful,

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.570
diverse, and strange land

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:14.010
where the waves meet the mountains,

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:15.550
where people follow their dreams,

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:17.883
or lose their minds or both.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:22.360
So I made it back to this
humid peninsula jutting

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.660
into the Gulf of Mexico.

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:26.340
It's familiar, but not
quite the same as before.

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:28.560
I'm sure I'll have more to
say about you soon, Florida.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:30.160
With your terrifying reptiles,

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.690
and your COVID contrarianism,

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:32.980
and your lightning rod governor

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:36.070
who plays by different
rules for good and for ill.

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:39.450
The saying has been, "As goes
California, goes the nation."

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:42.190
Is that still true or is it Texas now?

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:44.600
Or is the importance of
geography simply diminished

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:45.720
in the network age?

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.400
Is Florida the future?

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:51.892
I don't really know, but it
is my future and my home.

